                        class="h-10 w-10 rounded-full bg-neutral-800 flex items-center justify-center hover:bg-blue-600 transition-colors duration-300">
                        <svg class="h-5 w-5 text-white" fill="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                          <path
                            d="M19 0h-14c-2.761 0-5 2.239-5 5v14c0 2.761 2.239 5 5 5h14c2.762 0 5-2.239 5-5v-14c0-2.761-2.238-5-5-5zm-11 19h-3v-11h3v11zm-1.5-12.268c-.966 0-1.75-.79-1.75-1.764s.784-1.764 1.75-1.764 1.75.79 1.75 1.764-.783 1.764-1.75 1.764zm13.5 12.268h-3v-5.604c0-3.368-4-3.113-4 0v5.604h-3v-11h3v1.765c1.396-2.586 7-2.777 7 2.476v6.759z">
                          </path>
                        </svg>
                      </a>
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>

                <div class="md:w-2/3">
                  <p class="text-neutral-700 text-lg italic mb-6">"Prof. Sudeep R. Bapat is an Assistant Professor in the Decision Sciences area at the Shailesh J.
                    Mehta School of Management, Indian Institute of Technology Bombay. He had his schooling
                    and undergraduate education in New Delhi. He obtained his Bachelor's degree in statistics
                    from the University of Delhi, a Master's in Science in applied statistics and informatics from
                    the Indian Institute of Technology, Bombay and Ph.D. from the University of Connecticut, USA
                    in 2017. His thesis mainly concentrates on estimation problems under a sequential sampling
                    strategy, which is beneficial under many practical real-world examples such as health studies,
                    ecology, and finance. He later worked as a Visiting Assistant Professor in the Probability and
                    Statistics Department of the University of California, Santa Barbara, and as an Assistant
                    Professor at the Indian Institute of Management, Indore. His current research interests extend
                    to other areas such as time series, censoring, change point detection, statistical psychology,
                    statistical finance etc. Prof. Bapat is currently also an associated faculty with the Centre for
                    Machine Intelligence and Data Science, the FedEX Centre for Advanced Logistics and Focused
                    Analytics, the National Disease Modelling Consortium, and the Centre for Defence Technology
                    Innovations and Strategies at IIT Bombay. He has presented talks as well as chaired and
                    organized sessions in many reputed national and international conferences in statistics, over
                    the years. He has written and published over 50 research papers in leading journals of the
                    field."</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

